  "observations": [
    "The native result visibly improves the source: coral rails now have broad controlled highlights and a rounded transverse value profile; slate slats have clear softened shoulders rather than thin dark marks on a flat field. The source horizontal top/bottom-rail identity is retained in N/S, with coherent rotated E/W presentations.",
    "Honey wood grain, rounded shoes, support construction and small attached brass pegs replace the source almost-black support blocks. Material separation stays readable at128/55 cells. At32, individual pegs simplify naturally while warm feet, blue deck and coral frame remain distinct.",
    "The rendered W belongs beside approved N/E/S. The actual five common material graphs, world, light rig, render response and registered camera match the approved native family. No viewpoint has a special grade, scale or highlight treatment.",
    "The full native and consumer phase matrices show stable structure and aligned seven-period deck motion. Directed W ports and compatible N/E/S rotations continue the same flow. Repeated and mixed routes show no material seam, new cap, collar, closing bar, gap, alternating tint, halo, clipping or dead black area.",
    "Actual cream-floor, gray, dark, light and transparency evidence was inspected. Browser playback at normal55 and phone32 does not reveal join shimmer, a phase reset or a loop pop. Enlarged native source images show clean construction rather than a target image card."
  ],
